---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Existing Projects" sectionLabel="Existing Projects" activeSlug="existing-project">
  <section class="section" id="existing-projects">
    <span class="section-label">Existing Projects</span>
    <h2>Using VibeCrew with Existing Projects</h2>
    <p>VibeCrew isn't only for greenfield work. Bringing it into an existing codebase provides structure, quality gates, and continuous improvement to projects that were started without this framework.</p>

    <h3>Onboarding an Existing Project</h3>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h4>Install the plugin</h4>
        <p>Same process as a new project: copy or symlink <code>claude-plugin-vibe-crew/</code> into your project root, then run <code>/setup</code> inside Claude Code.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Run /onboard</h4>
        <p>The <code>/onboard</code> command launches the <strong>Code Auditor agent</strong> in a read-only worktree to analyze your codebase. It supports 7 languages (Node.js, Python, Ruby, Go, Rust, PHP, Java) and:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Detects language and framework</strong> &mdash; scans manifests (<code>package.json</code>, <code>pyproject.toml</code>, <code>Gemfile</code>, <code>go.mod</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code>, etc.)</li>
          <li><strong>Extracts conventions</strong> &mdash; naming patterns, formatters, linters, commit format, import style</li>
          <li><strong>Identifies test gaps</strong> &mdash; compares source vs test files, finds untested modules, estimates coverage</li>
          <li><strong>Derives the design system</strong> &mdash; extracts existing CSS variables, colors, and spacing values via <code>extract-design-system.sh</code></li>
          <li><strong>Generates CLAUDE.md</strong> &mdash; project-specific rules from discovered patterns, framework conventions, and architecture</li>
          <li><strong>Initializes state</strong> &mdash; sets <code>foundation.complete = true</code> so the phase gate is unlocked immediately</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Or run /new-project for full foundation</h4>
        <p>Alternatively, when <code>/new-project</code> detects an existing codebase, it adapts the Tier 1 flow: the Stack Scout documents the stack as it exists (rather than researching from scratch), the design system is derived from existing CSS, and VISION.md is still generated from your input. This takes longer but produces all 6 foundation artifacts (VISION.md, design-system.css, TDR, roadmap, architecture diagrams, CLAUDE.md).</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Map existing features to the backlog</h4>
        <p>Use <code>/plan-features</code> to document features that already exist (marked as "complete") and define new features you want to build. This gives you a unified backlog that includes both history and future work.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h4>Start developing with full VibeCrew workflow</h4>
        <p>From this point forward, every new feature uses the Tier 2 cycle. The phase gate is active, the Performance Coach runs at session end, and CLAUDE.md accumulates project-specific intelligence.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <Callout type="info" title="The phase gate and existing code">
      <p>The phase gate only blocks <em>new</em> source code writes before the foundation is complete. Once you've completed the /new-project flow for your existing project, the gate unlocks and you can modify any file freely. Existing code is never touched or reformatted without your explicit instruction.</p>
    </Callout>

    <h3>What You Get Immediately</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Interrupt Protocol</strong> &mdash; native notifications for blocked agents, completed tasks, and errors</li>
      <li><strong>Safety hooks</strong> &mdash; protection against <code>rm -rf</code>, force pushes, and other destructive commands</li>
      <li><strong>Auto-formatting</strong> &mdash; every file the AI writes is formatted automatically via PostToolUse hooks</li>
      <li><strong>Context warnings</strong> &mdash; alerts at 60% and 80% context usage to prevent exhaustion</li>
      <li><strong>Cost tracking</strong> &mdash; real-time session cost via <code>/cost</code> with configurable spend limits</li>
      <li><strong>Status bar</strong> &mdash; persistent display of context %, cost, feature, Vibe Score, duration, and compactions</li>
      <li><strong>Security auditing</strong> &mdash; OWASP Top 10 scanning via <code>/audit</code> with language-specific dependency checks</li>
      <li><strong>Performance coaching</strong> &mdash; Vibe Scores and CLAUDE.md mutations from your first <code>/wrap</code></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
